              <li><code>claude-opus-4-20250514</code></li>
              <li><code>claude-sonnet-4-5</code> (the March refresh was sunset together with the original)</li>
              <li><code>claude-opus-4-5</code></li>
            </ul>

            <p>Anthropic does <strong>not</strong> auto-redirect retired IDs. The SDK and REST endpoint both raise <code>NotFoundError</code> immediately. If your application has any hardcoded <code>"claude-sonnet-4"</code> strings — in source code, environment variables, Kubernetes ConfigMaps, or feature flags — they will fail silently in production with no fallback. That's the failure mode this guide prevents.</p>

            <h2>Replacement Map</h2>
            <p>The table below covers every retired ID and the recommended replacement as of June 26, 2026. Pricing is per million tokens; cache reads are 10x cheaper than fresh input.</p>

